      "Waganakising Odawa communities remain in the region; the bay was never a vacant postcard. Mission and mill towns overwrote village sites still known in oral history.",
      "Hannah, Lay, and other mill names built the brick downtown. Once the white pine was cut, cutover land went to farms. Perry Hannah's town plan and the asylum (later a state hospital campus) gave the city institutional bones unusual for a lumber port.",
      "Cherry production concentrated on Old Mission and Leelanau peninsulas because those slivers of land are almost islands of lake climate. Processors and brine tanks made a commodity; tastings rooms later made a lifestyle. Migrant farm labor is part of every honest harvest account.",
      "The 1980s–2000s wine boom used the same thermal logic. Recent polar-vortex winters and low-ice springs have damaged buds and nerves. Traverse City's prosperity is now more visitor and healthcare than pie filling, but the trees are still the landscape's argument.",
